g up to the elephant and touching  its side and you feel its skin and  surprisingly it's so soft its hairs are  soft its skin is soft and kind of giving  in well that you've done a some  visualization but not just visualization  you've also done we might call it  tactile ization as well that's  imagination right intellection is going  to be something a bit different and so  Descartes is going to tell us early on  that if I consider closely what  imagination is I find that it's nothing  other than a certain application of the  Faculty that knows two bodies that are  intimately present to it and therefore  that they exist this is where we're  going with this that's the upshot of  that but first he says we really need to  think about what the difference between  imagination and pure intellection and  conception is so he says let's do  geometry here imagine a triangle not  hard to do right you just kind of draw  three lines in your head or maybe you  just popped it into your head right now  so that's one way of grasping what a  triangle is as a matter of fact we can  put one right here on the board right  here is a nice little triangle in case  you're having trouble imagining it you  can just look at that one right there so  he says when I imagine a triangle  I don't conceive only a figure composed  and comprised of three lines but but you  know beyond that I consider these three  lines like as if they're present by the  force and an inner application of my  mind I think of them I place them here  in my mind and he says that's properly  what I call imagining but what I want to  think of and here he brings up a term  that you're probably not familiar with a  killing on alright what is it killing on  well it comes from the Greek word 4000  right a thousand sided figure try to  imagine that now try to bring before  your mind a figure that has a thousand  sides I dunno if it has a thousand sides  did you just put together in your mind  something that is a whole bunch of sides  and it's almost like a circle and maybe  it's actually like a hundred sided  figure maybe it's a thousand in one  sided figure unless you can actually  count them in your head which is very  very tough to visualize you're not sure  that you actually have a killing on  there he says when I want to think of a  kill agon I can easily conceive of the  truth that it's a figure composed of a  thousand sides as easily as I conceive  of a triangle is a figure composed of  three sides but when I try to imagine  the thousand sides of a Killa Gong like  I do with the three of a triangle  to think of them as present with the my  the eyes of the mind what happens  he says following the custom that I have  to use my imagination all the time when  I think of corporeal things it happens  that in conceiving of a Killa gonn I  represent within my mind  he says a figure that is confusedly  representing this right confusedly as a  problem why because that's the opposite  of distinctly I need to have clear and  distinct ideas for Descartes  right but I don't have a clear and  distinct idea of a Killa God in the  sense that I imagined it I can't I can't  have a clear and distinct idea when I'm  going away from the senses going away  from diagrams and just conceiving of it  thinking about its properties when I'm  using this higher part of my mind and  going away from trying to picture it so  he says that it's you know very evident  that this figure is not a killing on  since it doesn't differ at all from what  I would represent if I think of a Miriah  GaN or some other figure with many sides  so this doesn't help me to discern what  the properties are of the Gilligan what  about if I think of a Pentagon well  that's a little bit easier right can you  imagine a Pentagon sure picture you know  one of those things on the soccer ball  there's hexagons and pentagons on soccer  balls or just think of the Pentagon  think of the the place where we have the  US military command and all that ot